{
  "_comment": [
    "A worked offline map plan, sized to fit a 2 GB package. Run it with:",
    "    bin/tile_prefetch --plan config/offline-map-plan.json --cache maps --dry-run",
    "and drop --dry-run once the total looks right.",
    "",
    "Each region names its own level range per layer, and a layer left out is",
    "not fetched there at all. That asymmetry is the whole point: a city is",
    "flat and wants imagery, a mountain range wants elevation, and the ocean",
    "wants neither beyond the global base. Every level costs four times the",
    "one below it, so reach for more regions before more levels.",
    "",
    "Levels in metres per pixel at the equator: z6 2446, z7 1223, z8 612,",
    "z10 153, z11 76, z12 38, z14 9.6, z15 4.8 (the deepest elevation there is)."
  ],
